# Who appears as the author of a commit an agent makes here.
#
# Left to itself, Claude Code commits as `Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>`.
# That address belongs to the GitHub account `claude`, so every such commit
# is counted towards that account in this repository's contributor
# statistics rather than towards the person who asked for the change and
# owns it.
#
# This table maps the signed-in person (environment variable
# CLAUDE_CODE_USER_EMAIL) to the git identity to record as the *author*.
# The address must be registered with that person's GitHub account —
# either their primary address or <id>+<login>@users.noreply.github.com —
# or GitHub attributes the commit to nobody at all.
#
# The *committer* stays the agent and every commit keeps its
# `Co-Authored-By:` trailer, so where the change came from is still on the
# record. What moves is only who GitHub counts it for.
#
# Format (one entry per line, `#` starts a comment):
#   <CLAUDE_CODE_USER_EMAIL> = <git name> <<git email>>

